# Fixed 2026-09-29, defect 130's class, lane X4. Symptom: the members of a
# record, a variant or an `extern` group written in braces, `record Point {`
# over `x: i64,` over `y i64,` over `}`, went whole after the `{`'s one
# report, so `y i64` was never told (lane X1's finding 1); a record in braces
# on one line, `record Pair { left: i64, right i64 }`, was named empty with
# its fields there; and junk before the `{`, `record Junk ) {`, cost
# `empty_record` and then `expected_declaration` at the `}`. Cause: the
# braced region was skipped `{` to `}`, where a body in braces under any head
# that owes one was read. The members are now read through a view of the
# braces laid out as an indented block (`parse/braced_lines.hero`), the `,`
# between them and the `}` the habit's debris: under the head's one report
# of the `{`, each member's own mistake is told, a group's signatures and a
# record nested in a braced group too, and junk before the `{` is told as
# junk, the `{` then where it stands. Braces that hold nothing hold no member
# either, and that is told beside them.

record Point {  #~ expected_end_of_line
    x: i64,
    y i64,  #~ expected_field_type
}

variant Shade {  #~ expected_end_of_line
    light, 5,  #~ expected_case
    grey
}

record Pair { left: i64, right i64 }  #~ expected_end_of_line expected_field_type

record Nothing {}  #~ expected_end_of_line empty_record

record Junk ) {  #~ expected_end_of_line empty_record
    a: i64
    b i64  #~ expected_field_type
}

extern "m.h" {  #~ expected_end_of_line
    function q() -> i64
    function r(x i64) -> i64  #~ expected_parameter_type
    record S {  #~ expected_end_of_line
        a: i32,
        b i32,  #~ expected_field_type
    }
}

function main()
    print(1)
